{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The War Within and Ascendancy feel like natural next choices because their aggressive vocals and melodic riffs connect with what draws me to Advance And Vanquish and Colony.",
    "Mezmerize and Vol. 3 appeal to me because they combine heaviness with memorable melodies, connecting my interest in Ten Thousand Fists with the more adventurous sound of 10.000 Days."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Lonely Position of Neutral leans too far toward softer alternative rock for what I want right now, even though it connects with some of my earlier listening.",
    "Trapt and Natural Selection fit part of my taste, but their accessible hard rock sound is less compelling today than the heavier choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past interest in melodic hard rock seems to be treated as equally relevant to my current appetite for heavier music.",
    "Several albums fit the same broad mood, but that alone does not make me want all of them now; I would choose Ascendancy before also choosing The Crusade."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of aggression and melodic detail matters more to me right now than simply sounding like rock albums I have heard before.",
    "An album can fit my taste without becoming an immediate choice: Curse and Lost and Found interest me, but The War Within and Ascendancy give me stronger reasons to listen first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy music with strong melodies, but give too much weight to softer past listening and do not fully distinguish current priorities from general compatibility."
}"}
